{Rubinstein's Immortal. Two bishops on open diagonals, rooks on the open files, and a queen sacrifice that leaves White's whole army unable to help its king. Move list checked against Wikipedia.}
1. d4 d5 2. Nf3 e6 3. e3 c5 4. c4 Nc6 5. Nc3 Nf6 6. dxc5 Bxc5 7. a3 a6 8. b4 Bd6 9. Bb2 O-O 10. Qd2 Qe7 11. Bd3 dxc4 12. Bxc4 b5 13. Bd3 Rd8 14. Qe2 Bb7 15. O-O Ne5 16. Nxe5 Bxe5 17. f4 Bc7 18. e4 Rac8 {Both black rooks are on open or half-open files; both bishops point at the white king.} 19. e5 Bb6+ 20. Kh1 Ng4 {The attack begins. White's queen is overloaded: it guards g4 and the bishop on d3 at once.} 21. Be4 Qh4 22. g3 Rxc3 {The first sacrifice: the knight on c3 guarded e4.} 23. gxh4 Rd2 {The second: the queen is offered, and White cannot take anything.} 24. Qxd2 Bxe4+ 25. Qg2 Rh3 {Mate on h2 cannot be stopped. White resigned.} 0-1
